# Contextual Guidance Test

This workflow verifies the optional post-creation guidance tips
(r[guidance-tips]): helpful for beginner and LLM users, and silent when
they would be noise.

## Create in a project without epics

The fixture store has no epics yet: creation must print nothing extra
after the issue detail (no epic tip, no epic list, no dependency tip).

```console
$ pebbles new "First bug" --issue-type bug
Created bug [..]
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ID: [..]
Title: First bug
Type: Bug
Status: PROPOSED

Created: [..]
Updated: [..]
File: bug-[..]-first-bug.json
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

```

## Create the first epic

Creating an epic itself never suggests the epic link (an epic cannot be
part_of another epic, r[part-of-epic-types]): no epic tip, no epic list.
The dependency tip still applies, since a fresh epic has no relationships.

```console
$ pebbles new "Platform epic" --issue-type epic
Created epic [..]
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ID: [..]
Title: Platform epic
Type: Epic
Status: PROPOSED

Created: [..]
Updated: [..]
File: epic-[..]-platform-epic.json
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Tip: Add dependencies with: pebbles link [..] required_for <other-id>

```

## Create a bug now that an epic exists

The project has one epic: creation suggests the epic link, lists the
pickable epic (id + title), and still offers the dependency tip.

r[verify guidance-tips]
```console
$ pebbles new "Second bug" --issue-type bug
Created bug [..]
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ID: [..]
Title: Second bug
Type: Bug
Status: PROPOSED

Created: [..]
Updated: [..]
File: bug-[..]-second-bug.json
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Tip: Link to an epic with: pebbles link [..] part_of <epic-id>
  [..] Platform epic
Tip: Add dependencies with: pebbles link [..] required_for <other-id>

```

## Create a usecase

Any creatable type that can be part of an epic gets the same guidance.

```console
$ pebbles new "Mobile usecase" --issue-type usecase
Created usecase [..]
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ID: [..]
Title: Mobile usecase
Type: Usecase
Status: PROPOSED

Created: [..]
Updated: [..]
File: uc-[..]-mobile-usecase.json
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Tip: Link to an epic with: pebbles link [..] part_of <epic-id>
  [..] Platform epic
Tip: Add dependencies with: pebbles link [..] required_for <other-id>

```

## Create another epic

Even with epics already present, creating an epic prints no epic tip.

```console
$ pebbles new "Design epic" --issue-type epic
Created epic [..]
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ID: [..]
Title: Design epic
Type: Epic
Status: PROPOSED

Created: [..]
Updated: [..]
File: epic-[..]-design-epic.json
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Tip: Add dependencies with: pebbles link [..] required_for <other-id>

```
